@startuml seq-notes-gap-decomposition
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the gap decomposition is about pages IN ORDER: a sequence diagram lays its
'' participants out left to right in declaration order (so page i is the i-th column, deterministically, with no
'' Graphviz involved), `box` groups the consecutive eligible pages of a gap, an arrow between two columns is "these
'' two pages are consecutive slides of the parse", and `==` dividers separate the parses being compared. Mermaid has
'' no LaTeX in labels and does not render byte-reproducibly.
'' Fills: orange = the pure notes model's objects (pages and gaps; gaps at the container tier); arrows: dark orange = a
'' step of the frame number the rules allow, red = a step they forbid (a choice that is not in the gap's choice set).
!include _vv-theme.iuml
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title The gap decomposition of the labels <latex>L = (1, 2, 3, 4, 2, 6, 3)</latex> — theory/12 §2.1

participant "page 0\n<latex>L_0 = 1</latex>\nrequired" as P0 IR_TINT
box "gap <latex>G_0</latex>: pages 1–3 (the plain run)" IR_FILL
participant "page 1\n<latex>L_1 = 2</latex>\neligible" as P1 IR_TINT
participant "page 2\n<latex>L_2 = 3</latex>\neligible" as P2 IR_TINT
participant "page 3\n<latex>L_3 = 4</latex>\neligible" as P3 IR_TINT
end box
participant "page 4\n<latex>L_4 = 2</latex>\nrequired" as P4 IR_TINT
box "gap <latex>G_1</latex>: page 5" IR_FILL
participant "page 5\n<latex>L_5 = 6</latex>\neligible" as P5 IR_TINT
end box
participant "page 6\n<latex>L_6 = 3</latex>\nrequired" as P6 IR_TINT

note over P0, P6
  Eligible pages (they carry their own physical page number, <latex>L_j = j + 1</latex>): 1, 2, 3, 5.
  Required slides (page 0, and every page that is not eligible): 0, 4, 6. The gaps lie between them.
end note

== parse 1 — gap <latex>G_0</latex> holds no block: candidate <latex>a = 1</latex> ==
P0 -[IR_BORDER]> P4 : a new frame, <latex>L_4 = L_0 + 1</latex>
rnote over P1, P3 : note pages of page 0
P4 -[IR_BORDER]> P6 : a new frame, <latex>L_6 = L_4 + 1</latex>
rnote over P5 : note page of page 4

== parse 2 — gap <latex>G_0</latex> holds the block <latex>[1, 1]</latex>: candidate <latex>a = 2</latex> ==
P0 -[IR_BORDER]> P1 : a new frame, <latex>L_1 = L_0 + 1</latex>
P1 -[IR_BORDER]> P4 : an overlay, <latex>L_4 = L_1</latex>
rnote over P2, P3 : note pages of page 1
P4 -[IR_BORDER]> P6 : a new frame, <latex>L_6 = L_4 + 1</latex>
rnote over P5 : note page of page 4

== every other choice of gap <latex>G_0</latex> breaks a rule ==
P0 -[ERROR_BORDER]> P2 : a block from page 2: <latex>L_2 = 3 \notin \{L_0, L_0 + 1\}</latex> (from page 3, the same)
P2 -[ERROR_BORDER]> P4 : the block <latex>[1, 2]</latex>: <latex>L_4 = 2 \notin \{L_2, L_2 + 1\}</latex>
P3 -[ERROR_BORDER]> P4 : the block <latex>[1, 3]</latex>, all slides: <latex>L_4 = 2 \notin \{L_3, L_3 + 1\}</latex>
note over P4, P6
  Gap <latex>G_1</latex> has one choice, no block: a block would have to start at a page
  <latex>x \in \{L_4 - 1, L_4\} = \{1, 2\}</latex>, before the gap. The tail after page 6 is empty.
end note

== the product of the choices ==
note over P0, P6
  <latex>C_0 = \{\varnothing, [1,1]\}</latex>, <latex>C_1 = \{\varnothing\}</latex>, <latex>C_2 = \{\varnothing\}</latex>: <latex>2 \cdot 1 \cdot 1 = 2</latex> valid parses, so the deck is :ambiguous —
  :candidates [1 2] (each parse's first note page in the run), :run-end 3, :base #{5} (the note pages
  every parse shares) and :fallback? false (the parse with no note page in the run, the block [1, 3],
  breaks rule 2). This is case (b1) of §2.3.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the pure notes model's pages and gaps; an arrow: consecutive slides whose labels obey rule 2 |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| consecutive slides whose labels break rule 2: that choice is not in its gap's choice set |
  An arrow joins two consecutive slides of a parse; every page it skips is a note page.
endlegend
@enduml
